solutions.explanation:
Because \(4=2^2\) and \(8=2^3\), both radicals can be written with the same positive base. Multiplying then adds their exponents:
\[
\sqrt[3]{4}\sqrt[4]{8}
=2^{2/3}2^{3/4}
=2^{8/12+9/12}
=2^{17/12}.
\]
Since \(17/12=1+5/12\), we can separate one factor of \(2\):
\[
2^{17/12}=2\cdot2^{5/12}
=2\sqrt[12]{2^5}
=2\sqrt[12]{32}.
\]
All bases are positive, so these fractional-power rules apply. The answer is \(2\sqrt[12]{32}\), choice E.
